:: BackgroundChase1
    <<passagestart>>\
    You take a second and think. You can remember a few things, but its almost like the rest of the memories are out of reach.

    You recall a forest, a campfire, and tents in a clearing. You were sitting at the campfire holding a cup of something. Coffee! It was coffee.

    You remember feeling cold, but renewed, sort of refreshed in the cold morning air.

    Beyond actual memories, that's all you could find. And then it hits you like a freight train and leaves you unable to think, or even to breath. Horror. Pure, unadulerated horror. For a moment all want is to flee and hide, but instead all you can do is stand frozen in place.

    Just as quickly as it came over you, you are freed from your unreasonable horror. You tell $npcs.barden.name.formal:

    <<nobr>>
        <div class='passage-links-grid-vertical-long'>
            <<button[[I was camping in the woods... | WakingUp7]]>>
                <<set $plrSpkChoice = "I was in the woods, camping. There might have been others there, but I don't remember anything else.">>
            <</button>>
            <<button [[Actually, I remember something completely different. | WakingUp6]]>><</button>>
        </div>
    <</nobr>>

